      "writtenOn": "2020-01-29T10:15:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed with the objections but here are some things to modulate them :\n• NAI#toShortString is great to call but it can\u0027t handle the null case (if only we had Kotlin...)\n• A method in NAI would make it available to everyone who can see NAI, while this is private. Not that there is much of a difference in practice. But really, NAI#name exists and is called all over the place.\n\nSo I moved the implementation of this method into NAI#toShortString and offered a public static method there to deal with nulls. I removed naiToString() also NAI#name(), both of which are not very useful in practice and should be moved to this.",
